Backing tracks live here as "<Title> - <Artist>.mp3".

pubspec.yaml declares this whole directory as an asset bundle, and Flutter
fails the build if a declared asset directory does not exist - so this
placeholder keeps it present while the folder is empty. Delete it once
there are real tracks here if you like; nothing reads it.

SongCatalogService.bundled lists which songs the app offers, and
SongAudioService resolves each one to this folder by that exact filename
convention. There is no registry: the name IS the link.
